From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 12:30:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] KQuickIconProvider: requestedSize is in device pixels

Qt Quick passes image providers a requestedSize that already includes the
device pixel ratio (QQuickImageBase::load, HandleDPR). QIcon::pixmap(QSize)
multiplies by the application's device pixel ratio again, so on a scale 3
screen every theme icon was rendered at 9 times the pixels it needed; with
a large sourceSize that became a multi-gigabyte pixmap. Ask for exactly the
requested pixels.
---
 src/kquickiconprovider.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/kquickiconprovider.h b/src/kquickiconprovider.h
--- a/src/kquickiconprovider.h
+++ b/src/kquickiconprovider.h
@@ -44,7 +44,7 @@
 
         QPixmap pixmap;
         if (requestedSize.isValid()) {
-            pixmap = QIcon::fromTheme(source.at(0)).pixmap(requestedSize);
+            pixmap = QIcon::fromTheme(source.at(0)).pixmap(requestedSize, 1.0);
         } else if (size->isValid()) {
             pixmap = QIcon::fromTheme(source.at(0)).pixmap(*size);
         } else {
